{% lede %}
I love capturing the playful spirit that brings joy to the world. These are studio portraits of clowns and performers, shot plainly so the character can do all the work.
{% /lede %}

No stage, no story: one person, a plain backdrop and whatever face they brought that day. A rubber-chicken headband and a deadpan stare say as much as a whole show.

Most of these are performers I've photographed on stage too, caught here between characters instead of mid-scene.
